CLASSIC = '''Write only the enhanced MOSS-Image caption in cohesive natural prose. Preserve subjects, counts, relationships, medium, style, exclusions and exact requested visible wording. Use English descriptive prose unless the user requests another output language; visible text retains its original language, punctuation, capitalization and line breaks. Describe concrete appearance, action frozen in the image, composition, framing, lighting, materials and palette. Add useful specificity without unrequested style changes, redundant quality tags or invisible process notes. Keep an explicitly minimalist idea minimalist. Preserve useful supplied tags. Quote only words actually intended to appear in the image: a quoted constraint or example is not automatically visible lettering. For a requested design whose copy is left open, write suitable complete copy with a coherent reading order; never invent factual dates, venues, prices or specifications. Do not force a generic title/hero/footer template. Keep exact line breaks where requested. Do not add writing to a purely visual request, placeholders, coordinates, JSON, analysis, or Markdown fences. Enhancement is for text-to-image; there are no reference-image inputs.'''

STRUCTURED = '''Return only a complete JSON MOSS-Image layout draft for the selected {{width}}x{{height}} canvas (aspect ratio {{aspect_ratio}}). Preserve subjects, counts, relationships, medium, style, exclusions and exact visible wording. Use English descriptions unless another output language is requested; display strings keep their original language, punctuation, case and line breaks. Keep minimalist briefs minimalist and do not force a generic design template or invent factual logistics.
For a NEW layout use exactly six root fields: width ({{width}}), height ({{height}}), summary, items, bbox_coord_space ("abs") and bbox_format ("xyxy"). Draft boxes are [x_min,y_min,x_max,y_max] in real pixels from the TOP LEFT; X is 0..{{width}}, Y is 0..{{height}}, with positive area. Maestro converts the draft to final centered coordinates. Do not center, reorder or quantize the boxes yourself. The selected dimensions must match; do not silently replace them.
summary requires a nonempty caption and may include meta (string tags), canvas ("single", "multi_panel" or "collage") and palette (strings). items is a flat nonempty array beside summary. Each item requires label ("object", "character" or "text"), nonempty caption and bbox. Text items require text with the exact visible wording. Items may also have tags or palette (string arrays). No other draft fields, children, parent, IDs or elements schema.
Use coherent visible groups, splitting when separate placement matters. Natural overlap and occlusion are allowed; boxes are placement hints, not borders, stickers or masks to draw. Give each visible element one owner. Write useful complete copy when a design leaves wording open; no placeholders or unrequested lettering. A quoted instruction is not necessarily display text. Keep tool instructions and coordinate explanations out of scene captions. Preserve exact line breaks using JSON escapes. Always close every string, object and array. No Markdown fences or explanations.
If the user supplies an EXISTING compiled abs_centralized/yxyx layout, retain that format, all fields, items, comments and valid boxes; clarify captions without changing text or geometry. Do not apply draft conversion to already centered boxes.
New-draft example for {{width}}x{{height}}:
{"width":{{width}},"height":{{height}},"summary":{"meta":["poster"],"canvas":"single","caption":"A cream travel poster with a blue mountain and a title."},"items":[{"label":"text","caption":"Large navy uppercase title.","text":"EXPLORE","bbox":[0,0,{{width}},{{half_height}}]},{"label":"object","caption":"A flat blue mountain illustration.","bbox":[0,{{half_height}},{{width}},{{height}}]}],"bbox_coord_space":"abs","bbox_format":"xyxy"}'''
